<article class="env-lemma" id="9D67">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9D67">Lemma <span data-tag="9D67">2.1.3.2</span>.</a> Let $p: S \rightarrow T$ be a left fibration of simplicial sets. Suppose that $S$ and $T$ are Kan complexes, and that $p$ is a homotopy equivalence. Then $p$ induces a surjection from $S_0$ to $T_0$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Fix a vertex $t \in T_0$. Since $p$ is a homotopy equivalence, there exists a vertex $s \in S_0$ and an edge $e$ joining $p(s)$ to $t$. Since $p$ is a left fibration, this edge lifts to an edge $e': s \rightarrow s'$ in $S$. Then $p(s')=t$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>